@flexiarg institutions/congruence-with-local-conditions
@title Congruence With Local Conditions
@keywords congruence, local conditions, time, place, technology, Ostrom 2A, common-pool resources
@audience institution designers, commons researchers
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade principle
@provenance Ostrom design principle 2A, wording as in Cox, Arnold and Tomas (2010), "A review of design principles for community-based natural resource management", Ecology and Society 15(4):38, quoted in Corneli 2016 (ICCC 2016) Table 1. Original source Ostrom 1990, Governing the Commons. Drafted by claude-16 with Joe, 2026-10-29.
@status draft 2026-10-29; to vet against Ostrom 1990 and Cox et al. 2010 before relying on non-quoted text
@references [institutions/ARGUMENT creativity-commons/process-fits-local-conditions]

! conclusion:
  "Appropriation and provision rules are congruent with local social and environmental conditions."

  + context:
    Ostrom (1990) breaks local conditions down along time, place, technology and quantity of resource units.

  + IF:
    Rules for use and upkeep are being chosen for a particular resource and community.

  + HOWEVER:
    Rules copied from elsewhere, or imposed uniformly across different places, are cheaper to write and easier to audit.

  + THEN:
    Fit the rules about withdrawal and upkeep to the local resource, technology and social arrangements, and revise them when those change.

  + BECAUSE:
    Uniform rules applied to different conditions fail where the conditions differ, and users then ignore or evade them.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Vet the HOWEVER and BECAUSE against Ostrom 1990 and Cox et al. 2010; only the conclusion is quoted.]
    next[Creativity-commons transposition: creativity-commons/process-fits-local-conditions.]
